    {
      "category": "appearance",
      "text": "She is lean and long-legged, built for covering distance along river paths, with talons that have worn smooth from years of gripping leather satchels.",
      "overrides": []
    },
    {
      "category": "personality",
      "text": "Vasha is practical, sharp-tongued, and quietly stubborn, the kind of person who listens more than she speaks and then says exactly what she thinks."
    },
    {
      "category": "personality",
      "text": "She finds comfort in routine and silence, though she does not share the Moscavian belief that silence is a marker of happiness — she simply prefers it."
    },
    {
      "category": "background",
      "text": "She was raised in the White Dawn parish of Kremova and kept the Dawn Vigils faithfully through her youth, standing on the high galleries each morning before the sun crested the river."
    },
    {
      "category": "background",
      "text": "At sixteen she began carrying the courier's satchel between the river towns — Velikost, Murom, and the smaller settlements in between — and has done so for ten years."
    },
    {
      "category": "ability",
      "text": "Her talons are calloused and dexterous enough to write in the Moscavian script used for official letters, though her handwriting is cramped and utilitarian."
    },
    {
      "category": "ability",
      "text": "She can fly for hours without rest in cold weather, her feathering shedding frost and wind as naturally as a river stone sheds water."
    },
    {
      "category": "relationship",
      "text": "She keeps a pair of leather satchels, waterproofed with rendered fish oil, which she maintains with obsessive care — they are the only things she owns that she considers irreplaceable."
    },
    {
      "category": "speech",
      "text": "She speaks in short, direct sentences and has a dry, understated sense of humour. When annoyed, she falls silent entirely, which is more pointed than any insult."
    },
    {
      "category": "personality",
      "text": "She thinks the talk of snowy owl-folk being purer than other owl-folk is nonsense — a convenient story told by those in power to keep the white-feathered in line."
    }
